# Lavish review artifacts (local HTML review surfaces; not source)
.lavish/

# Relocated document subtrees, mounted locally by `npm run docs:mount`.
#
# These live in the external documents repository now. The mount is a symlink,
# and a symlink stores its target as content — committing one would hard-code
# one machine's layout into every checkout and dangle for everyone else. A
# dangling link is worse than an absent directory: a tree walk sees an entry
# and fails on read instead of skipping it.
#
# One line per relocated subtree, so a subtree that has NOT been relocated is
# still tracked normally and `docs:mount` refuses to shadow it.
#
# NO TRAILING SLASH. A trailing slash matches a DIRECTORY, and the mount is a
# SYMLINK — which git treats as a file. Written as `docs/audits/` these
# patterns matched nothing, the links were committed with mode 120000, and
# their content was one machine's relative path, which dangles everywhere else.
docs/adrs
docs/architecture
docs/assets
docs/audits
docs/bugs
docs/contexts
docs/designs
docs/followups
docs/guides
docs/market
docs/migrations
docs/plans
docs/proposals
docs/rca
docs/refactors
docs/references
docs/research
docs/runbooks
docs/specs
